			)
		)
		(uuid "dbc7f541-5d97-448b-9edd-1d9183a620fb")
	)
	(text_box "POT to set duty cycle\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 197.104 155.194 0)
		(size 23.114 3.302)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1296abd5-adff-4420-bd7e-191257d3de9c")
	)
	(text_box "Synchronous Buck Converters replace the diode in the smoothing network with a secondary MOSFET that works opposite of the primary switching MOSFET. Requires a MOSFET driver controller and an MCU to manage the duty cycles. Improves overall efficiency of converter."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 26.67 0)
		(size 127.508 7.62)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
				(color 200 0 30 0.9411764706)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4ab67a8c-2000-43a1-8f3c-3b3c1d31a974")
	)
	(text_box "This is a rather common design for Buck Converters, with most having an efficiency of ~75% depending on component quality.\nLosses in this design can be found in:\n- MOSFET conduction and switching loss\n- Diode forward-voltage loss\n- Component ESR\n- Feedback resistor divider\n- Indicator LEDs\nWith severity of loss getting less and less critical as we move down. Some losses are already minimized thanks to optimized ICs such as the MOSFETS losses, but other portions may have real impact."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.812 137.414 0)
		(size 118.364 21.844)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 0 30 0.94)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "55b4d3e5-d12c-42fb-a443-f5a4680be6ab")
	)
	(text_box "LM2596 outputs a PWM signal. It attempts to keep FB pin at 1.23V by adjusting the output duty cycle. As such the voltage divider circuit we have will force the FB higher/lower and the output will adjust to compensate."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.812 124.46 0)
		(size 89.154 8.128)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "59b06b09-14f4-40c3-8068-d426a4e4d531")
	)
	(text_box "Buck converters, converter a DC singal into a PWM signal with average voltage equal to our desired output.\n- Inductor smooths ripple current\n- Output capacitor smooths ripple voltage.\n- Input capacitors smooths input current by having it charge during off switch\n- Diode (1N5819) provides a path for inductor to discharge through\nVout = Vin*DutyCycle"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.812 40.894 0)
		(size 113.03 13.97)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "78d0c66c-a3e7-4ddf-8253-057b166c76fc")
	)
	(text_box "\"Optional Decoupling Cap\" \n- Reduce ESR and ESL\n- High Frequency Filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 112.522 125.476 0)
		(size 22.606 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ba9bc554-5358-4ea7-87bc-8ba2fb35187a")
	)
	(text_box "Gate Pull-down Resistors : Ensures MOSFET is firmly off when not driven. Gate is effectively a capacitor and can retain charge from past cycles. Pull-down continously discharges gate and protects from EMI(larger values = slower discharge).\n\nBootstrapping Circuit : The bootstrap diode charges a capacitor while the switch node is low. The charged capacitor then powers the floating high-side gate driver, allowing it to drive the MOSFET gate several volts above its source as the source voltage rises. The capacitor is refreshed each time the switch node returns low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 155.702 105.41 0)
		(size 127.508 13.97)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e9ae2f5b-7e5d-4595-99b9-5f85dd0f5f69")
	)
